  "notes": [
   "Pieces and edges are only a best reading of the small step diagrams on page 1 (steps 1-6). The positions of the bricks, bracket, mudguard and plates are partly guessed.",
   "The minifigure (Emma) shown on the page is not in the parts list, so it is not recorded.",
   "Step 2 is read as two pink grooved tiles. The third pink tile is expected on a later page.",
   "In step 4 I assumed the white bracket sits on the grey 2x2 plate. The grey plate is hidden under it afterwards.",
   "The pieces in the wheel area of step 6 could not be identified, so I added no wheel arch, wheels or tyres. They are expected on the next page.",
   "The output schema has no `pieces`/`rests_on` fields, so I used `parts` and `joined` edges instead. My page 1 reply was left empty by mistake. I have therefore included the page 1 pieces (b1-b15) here along with page 2, so this reply holds the whole model.",
   "Page 2 has step 7 (the third pink tile goes on the front) and step 8 (the minifigure sits in the car). Step 8 also shows the wheels, but I could not see how they were fitted. I placed the four wheels (b21-b24) and four tyres (b25-b28) there. I also placed the windscreen (b16), wheel arch (b17), grille tile (b18) and pink panel (b19), which do not clearly appear on page 1.",
   "Where each piece sits is a best guess from small drawings. The wheel pin and stud port names are not named, so the edges have no ports.",
   "The minifigure is not in the parts list, so it is not recorded."
  ]
